        {
          "pseudo_id": "p3",
          "pseudo": "The cancellation of the examination and its rescheduling represent a rupture in the normal flow of credentialization. For the governing body, it is a restoration of procedural legitimacy. For the examinee cohort, it is a forced re-entry into a high-stakes, anxiety-producing process. The arrests signal the center's capacity to discipline its periphery, while the rescheduled date reimposes the timeline of institutional power upon millions of individual ambitions.",
