          "pseudo_id": "p1",
          "pseudo": "It all began with a misplaced PDF. In the chaotic shuffle of files after the exam, a single email attachment, containing a chemistry paper identical to the official one, was sent to the National Testing Agency. This wasn't a grand leak, but a trivial misdirection—perhaps a file saved to the wrong folder, or an attachment meant for a different recipient. That one digital misstep, four days after the test, unraveled the entire NEET-UG 2026. The agency's systems flagged the match, launching a trace back to the 26-27 paper setters and translators. Thirteen arrests and a cancelled exam later, the chaos traces back not to a mastermind, but to a single, easily-ignored click.",
